+through binary64 and calls the host square root. Software and hardware-assisted Universal rows
+are separate series.
+
+## Reading the output
+
+The FloatLean lines can change kernel as the width changes. The plot breaks a line at each backend
+boundary and labels the segments `R###`. `backend-regimes.csv` maps those labels to the concrete
+backend, format range, and operation.
+
+A complete result contains:
+
+- every per-row CSV and aggregate trial CSV;
+- calibration pilots and selected iteration counts;
+- process memory and timing records;
+- CPU, operating-system, load, compiler, dependency, source, and executable information;
+- summary and ratio tables;
+- PNG, SVG, and PDF plots;
+- `MANIFEST.tsv`, with the size and SHA-256 digest of every retained artifact.
+
+The external executables identify what ran, but they do not become part of FloatLean's proof base.
+
+## Historical checked-in result
+
+[`results/main/`](../results/main/) is retained as a historical snapshot. It combines runs made
+with the old benchmark protocol, including counter-indexed loops, three-trial cells, and
+overlaid result directories. The current parser rejects that raw schema. Do not cite it as a
+measurement of the current tree.
+
+`benchmarks/scripts/verify-main-result.sh` checks that the historical files still match their
+recorded hashes. It does not upgrade them into current benchmark evidence.
