+## Independent sources
+
+We do not call something an external check without naming where it came from. These are the
+upstream sources used by the maintained adapters:
+
+| What we check | Source we use |
+| --- | --- |
+| IEEE arithmetic and flags | [Berkeley TestFloat](https://github.com/ucb-bar/berkeley-testfloat-3) with [Berkeley SoftFloat](https://www.jhauser.us/arithmetic/SoftFloat-3/doc/SoftFloat.html) |
+| Low-bit interchange values | [ONNX float8 specification](https://onnx.ai/onnx/technical/float8.html) |
+| Configurable low-precision values | [IEEE P3109 public tables](https://github.com/P3109/Public) |
+| Binary arithmetic and rounding | [GNU MPFR manual](https://www.mpfr.org/mpfr-current/mpfr.html) |
+| Ball and transcendental arithmetic | [Arb](https://arblib.org/) through [python-flint](https://python-flint.readthedocs.io/) |
+| Independent posit execution | [Stillwater Universal](https://github.com/stillwater-sc/universal) |
+| Proved binary reference execution | [Flocq](https://flocq.gitlabpages.inria.fr/) |
+| Ordinary Python float execution | [CPython float API](https://docs.python.org/3/c-api/float.html) and [`math.fma`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/math.html#math.fma) |
+
 TestFloat and MPFR call logical `Model` operations: status-bearing arithmetic uses
 `*WithStatus`, comparisons use `Model.compare`, and binary16 rows use `Model.add` or `Model.mul`.
 They do not invoke configured backends. The dedicated `lake -d tests exe check native` suite
